.TH "CSSUNITVALUE.UNIT" "3JS" "August 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSUnitValue.unit \- CSSUnitValue: unit property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]unit\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] interface returns a string indicating the unit
type.
.SH VALUE
A string indicating the unit type, such as \f[CR]\(dqem\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqpx\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dq%\(dq\f[R], etc.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
The following code creates a \f[CR]CSSPositionValue\f[R] from individual
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] constructors, then queries the
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue.unit\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] pos = \f[B]new\f[R] CSSPositionValue(
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnitValue(5, \(dqpx\(dq),
  \f[B]new\f[R] CSSUnitValue(10, \(dqem\(dq),
);

console.log(pos.x.unit); \f[I]// \(dqpx\(dq\f[R]
console.log(pos.y.unit); \f[I]// \(dqem\(dq\f[R]
.EE
